hen weight compression\n  is enabled. It uses a 56-thread OpenMP team, leaving eight cores for the\n  runtime. Its measured encode cost was approximately 0.8--1.3 ms per worker\n  call and was usually hidden off the GPU critical path.\n\nThe serving allocator's conservative combined K+V compressed-slot budget is\n51,248 B/block for CD3 and 65,554 B/block for P4Flat. P4Flat's actual normal\nblob stride is 25,600 B per K or V side, but its budget reserves raw-fallback\ncapacity. CD3 therefore received 16,345 offloadable blocks versus 14,561 for\nP4Flat; both were sufficient for this workload.\n\n## CD3 KV implementation exercised by this suite\n\n- Native batched encode, batched decode, and indexed batched decode.\n- Fixed Packed20 exception capacity with overflow validation.\n- Persistent host/GPU pools and metadata-only slot reclamation.\n- Dense-prefix H2D plus indexed decode for fragmented physical slots.\n- Full-block-only GPU-direct serving path.\n- CLI/backend registration and vLLM LPDDR budget integration.\n\nDefault exception capacity is 768 entries per block. A 1,024-block real-cache\nsample had maxima of 233 (K) and 197 (V). Native K/V round trips were bit-exact.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `tests/test_chunk_delta3.py tests/test_kv_prefill_load_policy.py`: 16 passed.\n- All 12 suite runs: exit code 0.\n- Final GPU utilization: 0%; no active model process.\n- Final 16 GiB hugepages: 23/23 free.\n\nThe next performance step for CD3 KV is a CPU-side CD3 encoder using the same\n`cpu_after_raw_swap` pipeline as P4Flat, or an equivalent scheduling change\nthat keeps GPU encode kernels off the fused-MM critical path.\n"}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA /home/ubuntu/cd3-offline-suite/results/20260831_182650/RESULTS.md\nA /home/ubuntu/cd3-offline-suite/results/20260831_182650/aggregate.tsv\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1788172328422,"completed_at_ms":1788172328423}}
